SNP 5/6 importance:- 

CORE FACTS:-
• Est. 1934 
• Massive growth after 2015, winning 56 out of 59 Scottish constituencies; 50% of the popular vote in Scotland 
• Won 35 seats in 2017 and 48 seats in 2019 – third biggest party in Westminster since 2015

IMPACT:- 
In Westminster… 
• SNP leaders in Westminster ask combative questions at PMQs 
• Large number of seats, so has a large influence when the governing party lacks a strong majority: 2016, SNP voted with Labour to block the Conservatives for longer store opening in England and Wales on Sundays 
• However, influence has been limited by Labour’s unwillingness to work too closely with the party who supplanted them in Scotland In government 

in Scotland… 
• Distinctive policies to those in England: free university tuition, free prescriptions, 16- and 17-yeard olds voting in some elections; have also pushed for a 2nd Independence referendum – without success 
• Limited by the UK Supreme Court: 2022 SC ruling that Nicola Sturgeon’s call for an independence referendum was illegal; 2017 Gina Miller case – SC ruled Scotland did not have to be consulted over EU withdrawal; 2023 Westminster govt blocked a Scottish govt bill relating to gender recognition, in the name of the Equality Act 2010

