UKIP/BREXIT/REFORM 6/6 importance:-
 
CORE FACTS:-
Est. 1993 
• Little impact until the 2004 European Parliament elections where it achieved 16.1% of the vote 
• Farage later founded the Brexit party in 2019 achieved 2% of the vote 
• In 2021 it rebranded as ‘Reform UK’ standing for ‘lower taxes, secure borders, cheaper energy and zero waiting lists

IMPACT:-
 • Little impact until the 2004 European Parliament elections where it achieved 16.1% of the vote 
 • Farage later founded the Brexit party in 2019 achieved 2% of the vote 
 • In 2021 it rebranded as ‘Reform UK’ standing for ‘lower taxes, secure borders, cheaper energy and zero waiting lists’ 
 • Nigel Farage became leader in 2006 and broadened its support among the white working class by opposing EU membership and opposing immigration 
 • The EU’s expansion and further immigration contributed to the party's growth 
 • Farage’s high profile media presence and ‘plain speaking’ and ‘common sense’ criticism of establishment politicians expanded UKIP’s influence further – 371.1k TikTok followers 
 • In the 2014 European Parliament elections, UKIP beat both Conservatives and Labour with 26.6% of the votes and 24 seats In Westminster... 
 • Tiny influence in parliament 
 • 2015 – 12.6% of the vote but 1 seat, 2017 – 1.8% of the popular vote but 0 seats 
 • Cameron’s 2015 promise of an ‘in/out’ referendum was made due to a growth of euroscepticism that UKIP fuelled 
 • Nigel Farage played a huge role in the 2016 EU referendum – placed promise on the free movement of EU citizens that mobilised working class voters towards leave 
 • Farage and UKIP greatly influenced policy around euroscepticism


THE GREEN PARTY 4/6 importance:-

CORE FACTS:-
• Originally known as PEOPLE and then the Ecology Party, changed its name to the Green party in 1985 
• 1989 – 15% of the vote in the European Parliament elections 
• 2010 – candidate Caroline Lucas won Brighton Pavilion for the Greens with 31.3%. 2019 – this became 57.2% 
• On average they have 3.6% of the vote in elections

IMPACT:-
• They have been able to sway support in constituencies by not standing. In 2019 they did not contest Ealing Central and Acton, so boosting the Labour vote at the expense of the Conservatives. In 2019, by not contesting North East Fife and Angus it swung towards LibDems and SNP instead of Conservatives 
• 2010 – candidate Caroline Lucas won Brighton Pavilion for the Greens with 31.3%. 2019 – this became 57.2% • On average they have 3.6% of the vote in elections 
• They have had greater influence in Scottish politics – in 2021 they secured 8/129 seats and the SNP secured 64 (one short of a majority) they formed a coalition. Two greens took ministerial positions and in a joint statement they came together to quell a climate emergency. They also had a mandate for a second independence referendum 
• They have greatly increased awareness of climate issues causing cross-party support for climate reforms in the 2019 election

DUP 2/6 importance:-

CORE FACTS:-
• Est. 1971 by Reverend Ian Paisley 
• Priority is to keep Northern Ireland as part of the United Kingdom 
• Strong links with the Free Presbyterian Church 
• Social conservatism and intense Protestantism that it defends have stopped it influencing mainstream parties

IMPACT:- 
• Played an indispensable role in the development of the peace process in Northern Ireland. Initially opposed to power sharing with republican parties, in the 2005 general election the DUP became the largest unionist party at Westminster 
• Ian Paisley’s 2007 decision to agree with power sharing with Sinn Fein was a pivotal event in the Northern Ireland peace process. 
• Their ideological differences and difficult relationship has caused issues in running government – 2017-2020 the Stormont assembly was suspended when Sinn Fein withdrew from the government 
• Gained strong influence in 2017 through a Confidence and supply agreement with the May government – meant they could stop the proposed Norhtern Ireland protocol this changed when the Conservatives gained an 80 seat majority in 2019 and they lost influence
